        "original_id": "d0c15d05-9797-535e-8e8c-9e3e0b843241",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Béla Bartók, Johann Christoph Pepusch, John Gay\n- Works: Rhapsody, Op. 1 (Bartók), The Beggar's Opera\n- Roles: composer, pianist, ethnomusicologist\n- Places: Hungary, England\n\nFacts:\n- Johann Christoph Pepusch was born in 1667 and died on 20 July 1752.\n- The Beggar's Opera is a ballad opera in three acts written in 1728 by John Gay, with music arranged by Johann Christoph Pepusch.\n- Béla Viktor János Bartók was born on 25 March 1881 and died on 26 September 1945.\n- Béla Bartók was a Hungarian composer, pianist, and ethnomusicologist.\n- Johann Christoph Pepusch, also known as John Christopher Pepusch and Dr Pepusch, was a German-born composer who spent most of his working life in England.\n- Rhapsody, Op. 1 (Bartók) is identified in the chunk as “1, Sz.”",
